Platform Engineer Interview Questions – Quick Prep Guide
If you're preparing for a Platform Engineer role, here are some key questions to focus on:

☁️ Cloud Infrastructure (AWS / GCP / Azure)
How do you design a scalable and highly available cloud architecture?
What’s the difference between EC2, Lambda, and Fargate?
How do you manage IAM roles and policies securely?
What are the best practices for multi-region deployments?

🧱 Infrastructure as Code (Terraform / CloudFormation / ARM)
How do you manage Terraform state files securely?
What’s the difference between Terraform modules and workspaces?
How do you handle drift detection in IaC?
How do you integrate Terraform with CI/CD pipelines?

🛠️ Configuration Management (Ansible / Puppet / Chef)
How do you ensure idempotency in Ansible playbooks?
What’s the difference between push and pull configuration models?
How do you manage secrets in configuration tools?

🐧 Linux System Administration
How do you troubleshoot high CPU usage on a Linux server?
What’s the difference between top, htop, and iotop?
How do you secure a Linux server?

🔁 CI/CD & DevOps Tools (Jenkins / Git / Maven)
How do you design a CI/CD pipeline for microservices?
What are the best practices for Jenkins pipelines?
How do you handle rollback in CI/CD deployments?

🗃️ Databases (PostgreSQL / Cassandra)
How do you optimize PostgreSQL queries?
What are the differences between Cassandra and PostgreSQL?
How do you handle schema migrations?

🐍 Scripting & Automation (Python / Bash / Java / Scala)
Write a Python script to monitor disk usage and send alerts.
How do you handle error logging and retries in Bash?
What are the advantages of using Scala in distributed systems?

📡 Messaging & Event-Driven Architecture (SNS / SQS / Kafka)
How do you design a decoupled system using SQS and SNS?
What are the differences between SQS and Kafka?
How do you ensure message durability and ordering?
